From 59a927377a753f622621841d8d1b845d24f80f30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:49:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): a down remote fails fast instead of redialing
 SSH per request [daveey]

On 2026-10-27 16:53-16:55 PDT the mini stopped answering: every renderer request opened its own SSH control
master and waited out the 15 s timeout, the next one dialing ~20 ms after the last failed (11 dials, 36 stalled
requests in 2 min). 0592's gate remembered only a remote's own-update refusal.

- remote-update-pause.ts: second failure class 'unreachable' with a written rule (classifyRemoteDialFailure):
  network (unreachable, timeout, transient-transport-error) and SSH refusals (auth-failed, interactive-auth,
  host-key-changed) are remembered per remote install with a 2/5/15/30/60 s backoff (prewarm's own steps);
  ssh-client-failed (#103288), superseded, post-dial remote states and untagged errors pass through. Cached
  errors keep message/kind/sshError so boot classifies them the same, plus code remote-unreachable-backoff and
  retryAt; the recorded error gets retryAt too. One probe per window; recovery logs once. clear(why) for
  explicit retries.
- main.ts: Reload and retry, Repair, connection apply/save and a reachable Test clear the gate so they dial at
  once; registry Reconnect and managed restores keep bypassing it via their correlation id.
- remote-dial-backoff.test.ts: renderer requests, prewarm and explicit reconnect paths, the classification table
  and the main.ts wiring.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
